[?2004l[?2004h> ### Delta sync recovery and merchandising data
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The sync applies changes in sequence order and commits each page together with
[?2004l[?2004h> its cursor, including empty and tombstone-only pages. If a later page fails,
[?2004l[?2004h> rerun `sync` to resume after the last committed page. Existing catalogs are
[?2004l[?2004h> migrated to one row per SKU (highest `feed_seq`, latest row on ties).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged; notice-acknowledgement responses are retried once
[?2004l[?2004h> at the same cursor. Notices do not authorize changes to local merchandising
[?2004l[?2004h> records. Feed tombstones remove products, not `price_overrides`; an active
[?2004l[?2004h> override continues to win if its SKU is later reissued. Review supplier notices
[?2004l[?2004h> about SKU reuse with merchandising and use the existing admin commands if an
[?2004l[?2004h> override should be ended. Sync never prunes or ends overrides automatically.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''; p.write_text(s)
